1
00:00:02,383 --> 00:00:04,177
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:06,429
Earth.

3
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:08,556
Fire.

4
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:10,683
Air.

5
00:00:11,309 --> 00:00:14,979
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,104 --> 00:00:18,816
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,359 --> 00:00:21,986
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,111 --> 00:00:23,404
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:26,866
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,283 --> 00:00:30,578
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

11
00:00:30,703 --> 00:00:32,622
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,747 --> 00:00:34,999
And although his airbending
skills are great,

13
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:37,710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,835 --> 00:00:39,045
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:42,423
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:58,151 --> 00:01:00,111
( SNORING )

17
00:01:00,237 --> 00:01:01,696
( CHATTERS )

18
00:01:05,742 --> 00:01:06,868
( BUZZES )

19
00:01:08,119 --> 00:01:09,120
Eh―

20
00:01:09,329 --> 00:01:10,330
( SQUEALS )

21
00:01:10,455 --> 00:01:12,040
( SPITTING )

22
00:01:12,165 --> 00:01:13,792
What are you doing in my mouth?

23
00:01:13,875 --> 00:01:14,876
( PURRS )

24
00:01:15,001 --> 00:01:17,963
Momo, you need to be a little
more sensitive to my boundaries.

25
00:01:18,046 --> 00:01:19,130
Ah!

26
00:01:20,131 --> 00:01:21,216
Huh?

27
00:01:23,385 --> 00:01:24,427
( GASPS )

28
00:01:25,929 --> 00:01:28,974
Give up. You're completely surrounded.

29
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:32,978
SOKKA: Come on! Come on, come on!

30
00:01:34,437 --> 00:01:36,064
My scrolls!

31
00:01:37,107 --> 00:01:38,566
My staff!

32
00:01:40,318 --> 00:01:41,361
Uh!

33
00:02:03,425 --> 00:02:04,467
Yip yip!

34
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:08,221
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

35
00:02:08,346 --> 00:02:09,723
Wait, my boomerang!

36
00:02:10,849 --> 00:02:11,891
There's no time!

37
00:02:11,975 --> 00:02:15,562
Oh, I see. So there's time to get
your scrolls, and time to get your staff,

38
00:02:15,645 --> 00:02:17,063
but no time for my boomerang?

39
00:02:17,188 --> 00:02:19,024
- That's correct.
- Oh...

40
00:02:23,987 --> 00:02:25,989
Sorry about your boomerang, Sokka.

41
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:28,616
I feel like I've lost part of my identity.

42
00:02:28,742 --> 00:02:30,493
Imagine if you lost your arrow,

43
00:02:30,618 --> 00:02:31,870
or if Katara lost her...

44
00:02:32,996 --> 00:02:34,539
Hair loopies.

45
00:02:36,791 --> 00:02:39,627
Here's your produce, pony tail guy.

46
00:02:39,753 --> 00:02:42,339
I used to be boomerang guy...

47
00:02:45,091 --> 00:02:47,093
Hey, Water Tribe money.

48
00:02:47,218 --> 00:02:48,470
I hope that's okay.

49
00:02:48,595 --> 00:02:50,555
So long as it's money.

50
00:02:52,807 --> 00:02:54,225
Have a nice Avatar Day!

51
00:02:54,351 --> 00:02:56,061
Avatar Day?

52
00:02:56,186 --> 00:02:58,229
You guys are going to the festival, right?

53
00:02:59,647 --> 00:03:01,399
( MUSIC PLAYING )

54
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,614
There's a holiday for the Avatar.

55
00:03:07,739 --> 00:03:08,782
Who knew?

56
00:03:08,907 --> 00:03:11,659
Look! They made a giant Kyoshi float.

57
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:15,789
SOKKA: And here comes Avatar Roku.

58
00:03:17,665 --> 00:03:21,252
Having a huge festival
in your honor is great, but frankly,

59
00:03:21,378 --> 00:03:23,213
it's just nice to be appreciated.

60
00:03:23,338 --> 00:03:26,633
And it's nice to appreciate
their deep-fried festival food.

61
00:03:26,758 --> 00:03:27,967
Aang, look!

62
00:03:28,176 --> 00:03:30,678
That's the biggest me I've ever seen.

63
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,896
They have a torch. That's a nice prop.

64
00:03:40,021 --> 00:03:42,482
It's bright, dangerous... ( SNIFFS )

65
00:03:42,607 --> 00:03:44,067
Smells manly.

66
00:03:44,192 --> 00:03:46,403
But I'm not sure I could carry it off.

67
00:03:46,528 --> 00:03:48,405
Hey, what's that guy doing?

68
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,781
( YELLS )

69
00:03:52,409 --> 00:03:54,285
CROWD: ( CHANTING ) Down with the Avatar!

70
00:03:54,369 --> 00:03:56,204
Down with the Avatar!

71
00:03:56,287 --> 00:03:58,373
Down with the Avatar!

72
00:04:05,713 --> 00:04:06,798
Uh! Uh!

73
00:04:27,152 --> 00:04:28,945
Where did you get these?

74
00:04:29,237 --> 00:04:31,364
What does it matter where they came from?

75
00:04:31,489 --> 00:04:32,657
Hmm...

76
00:04:34,576 --> 00:04:36,411
Mmm!

77
00:04:36,536 --> 00:04:38,037
CROWD: Down with the Avatar!

78
00:04:38,163 --> 00:04:39,831
Down with the Avatar!

79
00:04:41,791 --> 00:04:42,834
Uh!

80
00:04:45,795 --> 00:04:47,547
( CHEERING )

81
00:04:53,219 --> 00:04:55,972
That party-pooper's ruining Avatar Day!

82
00:04:58,057 --> 00:05:00,393
That party-pooper's my friend.

83
00:05:02,353 --> 00:05:04,272
It's the Avatar himself!

84
00:05:04,397 --> 00:05:07,525
MAN: It's going to kill us
with its awesome Avatar powers!

85
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:08,776
No, I'm not, I...

86
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,361
Aah! Aah! Oh, ho, ho!

87
00:05:11,738 --> 00:05:13,615
I suggest you leave.

88
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,658
You're not welcome here, Avatar.

89
00:05:15,783 --> 00:05:18,411
Why not? Aang helps people.

90
00:05:18,536 --> 00:05:20,914
It's true. I'm on your side.

91
00:05:21,122 --> 00:05:23,333
I find that hard to swallow,

92
00:05:23,416 --> 00:05:26,336
considering what you did to us
in your past life!

93
00:05:26,711 --> 00:05:28,671
It was Avatar Kyoshi.

94
00:05:28,796 --> 00:05:31,883
She murdered our glorious leader,
Chin the Great.

95
00:05:32,342 --> 00:05:33,593
You think that I...

96
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,220
Murdered someone?

97
00:05:35,345 --> 00:05:38,389
We used to be a great society
before you killed our leader.

98
00:05:38,515 --> 00:05:39,766
Now look at us!

99
00:05:40,141 --> 00:05:42,894
- Ah!
- Aang would never do something like that.

100
00:05:43,019 --> 00:05:44,604
No Avatar would.

101
00:05:44,729 --> 00:05:47,273
And it's not fair for you all
to question his honor!

102
00:05:47,607 --> 00:05:50,568
Let's tell her what we think
of the Avatar's honor!

103
00:05:50,693 --> 00:05:53,655
-( BLOWS RASPBERRY )
-( CHEERING )

104
00:05:54,989 --> 00:05:57,575
AANG: Give me a chance to clear my name.

105
00:05:57,951 --> 00:06:02,205
The only way to prove your innocence
is to stand trial.

106
00:06:02,539 --> 00:06:04,624
I'll gladly stand trial.

107
00:06:04,749 --> 00:06:07,001
You'll have to follow all our rules.

108
00:06:07,126 --> 00:06:09,796
That includes paying bail.

109
00:06:10,088 --> 00:06:11,339
No problem.

110
00:06:12,465 --> 00:06:15,718
How was I supposed to know
they wouldn't take Water Tribe money?

111
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:24,811
So some people don't like you, big deal.

112
00:06:24,894 --> 00:06:27,522
There's a whole nation
of firebenders who hate you.

113
00:06:27,605 --> 00:06:30,316
- Now let's bust you out of here.
- I can't.

114
00:06:30,692 --> 00:06:33,194
Sure you can! A little... ( BLOWS )

115
00:06:33,319 --> 00:06:35,530
Swish, swish, swish! Airbending slice!

116
00:06:35,863 --> 00:06:37,073
And we're on our way.

117
00:06:37,323 --> 00:06:40,034
KATARA: I think what Master Swish
Is trying to say,

118
00:06:40,159 --> 00:06:42,620
is that you're supposed
to be out saving the world.

119
00:06:42,704 --> 00:06:44,581
You can't do that locked up in here.

120
00:06:45,081 --> 00:06:48,001
I can't do that with people thinking
I'm a murderer, either.

121
00:06:48,084 --> 00:06:50,420
I need you guys to help
prove my innocence.

122
00:06:50,795 --> 00:06:54,132
How are we gonna do that?
The crime happened over 300 years ago.

123
00:06:54,549 --> 00:06:55,758
That's okay, Sokka.

124
00:06:55,842 --> 00:06:57,510
For some reason, I thought you were

125
00:06:57,635 --> 00:06:59,220
an expert detective.

126
00:06:59,721 --> 00:07:03,308
Well, I guess I could
be classified as such.

127
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:06,144
Yeah! Back home, he was famous for

128
00:07:06,227 --> 00:07:09,188
solving the mystery
of the missing seal jerky.

129
00:07:09,355 --> 00:07:11,691
Everyone wanted
to blame it on the polar leopard,

130
00:07:11,774 --> 00:07:13,610
but I figured out it was old man Jarco

131
00:07:13,693 --> 00:07:15,612
wearing polar leopard boots.

132
00:07:15,737 --> 00:07:19,240
See, a real 800 pound polar leopard
would've left much deeper tracks.

133
00:07:19,365 --> 00:07:21,618
Okay, I guess I am pretty good.

134
00:07:22,285 --> 00:07:23,870
So you'll help me with my case?

135
00:07:24,829 --> 00:07:27,624
Fine. But I'm gonna need some new props.

136
00:07:28,625 --> 00:07:30,335
I'm ready.

137
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,461
( LAUGHS )

138
00:07:31,586 --> 00:07:32,587
What?

139
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:34,339
( GRUNTING )

140
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:42,347
Uh!

141
00:07:43,264 --> 00:07:44,307
MAN: Ah! Uh!

142
00:07:49,479 --> 00:07:50,563
Whew.

143
00:07:50,647 --> 00:07:51,648
Eh, ah!

144
00:07:51,731 --> 00:07:52,815
Ahh!

145
00:07:58,696 --> 00:07:59,864
Ohh...

146
00:08:02,617 --> 00:08:05,119
MAYOR: This is the crime scene.

147
00:08:10,416 --> 00:08:14,003
This is the footprint of the killer,
Kyoshi.

148
00:08:14,128 --> 00:08:19,550
It was at sunset, 370 years ago today,

149
00:08:19,676 --> 00:08:24,055
that she emerged from the temple
and struck down Chin the Great.

150
00:08:24,764 --> 00:08:26,641
After that tragic day,

151
00:08:26,766 --> 00:08:28,017
we built this statue

152
00:08:28,142 --> 00:08:30,812
to immortalize our great leader.

153
00:08:31,312 --> 00:08:33,481
Feel free to appreciate it.

154
00:08:41,948 --> 00:08:45,159
This temple and this statue
were cut from the same stone.

155
00:08:45,868 --> 00:08:49,080
And we know that the statue
was built after Chin died.

156
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:52,208
So, if they were built at the same time,
that means―

157
00:08:52,291 --> 00:08:54,252
Shh! I wanna solve it!

158
00:08:54,502 --> 00:08:58,256
That means
Kyoshi never set foot in this temple.

159
00:08:58,339 --> 00:09:00,633
KATARA: That's a big hole
in the mayor's story,

160
00:09:00,717 --> 00:09:03,219
but it's not enough
to prove Aang's innocence.

161
00:09:03,636 --> 00:09:05,304
You're right.

162
00:09:08,141 --> 00:09:10,643
We need to go to Kyoshi island.

163
00:09:10,768 --> 00:09:12,603
Where'd you get that?

164
00:09:14,021 --> 00:09:15,106
( SNIFFING )

165
00:09:17,358 --> 00:09:18,651
( SQUEAKS )

166
00:09:18,776 --> 00:09:20,778
MAN: You got a bald head...

167
00:09:20,903 --> 00:09:22,447
Some nice tattoos.

168
00:09:23,906 --> 00:09:25,032
Argh!

169
00:09:25,116 --> 00:09:28,453
You're going to fit in
real well around here.

170
00:09:32,582 --> 00:09:33,708
( BELL RINGING )

171
00:09:35,376 --> 00:09:36,669
( LAUGHING )

172
00:09:39,213 --> 00:09:40,298
( GRUNTING )

173
00:09:41,549 --> 00:09:42,800
( CHEERING )

174
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:46,471
Ohh!

175
00:09:46,596 --> 00:09:49,474
( EXCLAIMING )

176
00:09:49,599 --> 00:09:52,602
( SCREAMING )

177
00:09:52,727 --> 00:09:54,479
( SPUTTERS )

178
00:09:58,941 --> 00:10:00,568
Where's Aangy?

179
00:10:00,985 --> 00:10:02,361
He couldn't be here, Koko.

180
00:10:02,945 --> 00:10:03,988
ALL: Oh...

181
00:10:04,071 --> 00:10:05,615
I want to see Aangy.

182
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:06,824
Oh.

183
00:10:17,168 --> 00:10:19,462
Oyaji, Aang is in jail.

184
00:10:19,587 --> 00:10:22,882
The town of Chin says he murdered
their leader in a past life.

185
00:10:23,007 --> 00:10:25,259
They say it was Kyoshi.

186
00:10:25,384 --> 00:10:27,762
Kyoshi? That's crazy talk.

187
00:10:27,887 --> 00:10:29,222
I'll take you to her shrine.

188
00:10:29,347 --> 00:10:32,517
Maybe something there
will help you clear her name.

189
00:10:34,936 --> 00:10:37,396
So, uh... What's Suki up to?

190
00:10:37,522 --> 00:10:39,106
Is she around?

191
00:10:39,232 --> 00:10:42,777
Actually, she and the other warriors
left to fight in the war.

192
00:10:43,319 --> 00:10:45,238
You kids had a big impact on Suki.

193
00:10:45,363 --> 00:10:47,198
She said you inspired her,

194
00:10:47,323 --> 00:10:49,784
and she wanted to help change the world.

195
00:10:50,117 --> 00:10:52,620
Oh, well... That's great.

196
00:10:54,622 --> 00:10:58,501
OYAJI: This temple was converted
into a shrine to Kyoshi.

197
00:10:58,626 --> 00:11:00,795
The clerics tell us these relics

198
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,381
are still connected to her spirit.

199
00:11:03,506 --> 00:11:05,091
That's her kimono.

200
00:11:05,216 --> 00:11:07,885
- She had exquisite taste.
- Please don't touch!

201
00:11:08,010 --> 00:11:09,595
SOKKA: These fans,

202
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,347
they were her weapons, no?

203
00:11:11,472 --> 00:11:14,684
Also refrain from touching the fans.

204
00:11:14,809 --> 00:11:18,020
These were her boots?
Her feet must have been enormous.

205
00:11:18,145 --> 00:11:19,272
( SQUEAKS )

206
00:11:19,397 --> 00:11:22,108
The biggest of any Avatar.

207
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:24,902
Wait a minute, big feet?

208
00:11:25,027 --> 00:11:26,404
Little footprints?

209
00:11:26,529 --> 00:11:27,572
There's no way!

210
00:11:27,697 --> 00:11:29,156
( CLEARS THROAT )

211
00:11:29,282 --> 00:11:31,325
Special outfit, hat and pipe...

212
00:11:31,450 --> 00:11:33,786
These things mean anything to you?

213
00:11:33,911 --> 00:11:36,747
You're right. I'm sorry. Please.

214
00:11:37,331 --> 00:11:38,332
Aha!

215
00:11:38,457 --> 00:11:41,502
There's no way Kyoshi could have
made that footprint.

216
00:11:41,627 --> 00:11:45,298
And therefore, there is nothing
linking her to the crime scene.

217
00:11:45,423 --> 00:11:47,008
Brilliant, Sokka.

218
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:53,848
This girl you're talking about,
she'll come around.

219
00:11:53,973 --> 00:11:55,474
You just gotta hang in there.

220
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,851
You think so?

221
00:11:56,976 --> 00:11:58,102
- Sure.
- Yeah.

222
00:11:58,227 --> 00:11:59,270
You're a catch.

223
00:11:59,395 --> 00:12:00,438
I don't know.

224
00:12:00,521 --> 00:12:01,522
Hey!

225
00:12:01,647 --> 00:12:04,358
You're smart, handsome, funny,

226
00:12:04,483 --> 00:12:06,652
not to mention you're the Avatar.

227
00:12:07,194 --> 00:12:08,446
You guys are great.

228
00:12:08,863 --> 00:12:11,490
Don't be afraid to tell her how you feel.

229
00:12:11,574 --> 00:12:12,658
( SNIFFS )

230
00:12:15,077 --> 00:12:18,414
This piece is called
"The Birth of Kyoshi."

231
00:12:18,581 --> 00:12:22,209
It was painted at sunrise
on the day this island was founded.

232
00:12:22,335 --> 00:12:26,964
Why, it was today, in fact, 370 years ago.

233
00:12:27,089 --> 00:12:29,258
( SPITS ) 370 years?

234
00:12:29,383 --> 00:12:31,385
Wait, are you sure it was today?

235
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:33,471
Well, seeing how it's Kyoshi day,

236
00:12:33,596 --> 00:12:35,598
yes, I'm sure.

237
00:12:36,474 --> 00:12:40,853
This ceremony didn't take place
at sunrise, it took place at sunset.

238
00:12:40,978 --> 00:12:42,563
Look at the shadows.

239
00:12:42,688 --> 00:12:45,983
They point east,
so the sun must have been in the west.

240
00:12:46,108 --> 00:12:48,277
- So what?
- Aah!

241
00:12:48,361 --> 00:12:50,279
If Kyoshi was in the ceremony at sunset,

242
00:12:50,363 --> 00:12:52,949
she couldn't have been in Chin
committing the crime.

243
00:12:53,532 --> 00:12:55,451
She has an alibi.

244
00:12:55,534 --> 00:12:56,869
Oh, uh!

245
00:12:57,620 --> 00:13:00,247
Honorable mayor,
we've prepared a solid defense

246
00:13:00,331 --> 00:13:01,332
for the Avatar.

247
00:13:01,415 --> 00:13:02,625
We did an investigation,

248
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:04,710
and found some very strong evidence.

249
00:13:05,211 --> 00:13:06,963
MAYOR: Evidence? Ha!

250
00:13:07,088 --> 00:13:09,340
That's not how our court system works.

251
00:13:09,632 --> 00:13:11,592
Then how can I prove my innocence?

252
00:13:11,717 --> 00:13:15,304
Simple. I say what happened,
and then you say what happened,

253
00:13:15,388 --> 00:13:18,349
and then I decide who's right.

254
00:13:18,474 --> 00:13:19,558
-( GASPS )
-( GASPS )

255
00:13:19,892 --> 00:13:23,521
That's why we call it justice,
because it's just us.

256
00:13:23,938 --> 00:13:25,773
( LAUGHING )

257
00:13:32,613 --> 00:13:34,407
Everyone loved Chin the Great,

258
00:13:34,532 --> 00:13:36,325
because he was so great.

259
00:13:36,534 --> 00:13:39,495
Then the Avatar showed up and killed him,

260
00:13:39,704 --> 00:13:41,872
and that's how it happened.

261
00:13:42,081 --> 00:13:46,335
The accused will now present its argument.

262
00:13:47,712 --> 00:13:50,172
You can do it, Aang.
Just remember the evidence.

263
00:13:50,297 --> 00:13:53,426
Right... Evidence.

264
00:13:53,551 --> 00:13:55,094
Ladies and gentlemen,

265
00:13:55,219 --> 00:13:57,638
I'm about to tell you
what really happened,

266
00:13:57,763 --> 00:14:00,433
and I will prove it with facts.

267
00:14:00,558 --> 00:14:02,351
Fact number one:

268
00:14:03,394 --> 00:14:05,104
Uh...

269
00:14:05,229 --> 00:14:06,564
The footprints.

270
00:14:06,689 --> 00:14:07,773
Oh, yeah.

271
00:14:08,357 --> 00:14:11,360
You see, I have very large feet.

272
00:14:14,155 --> 00:14:15,448
Furthermore,

273
00:14:15,906 --> 00:14:19,118
your temple... Matches your statue.

274
00:14:21,203 --> 00:14:24,290
But I was in a painting at sunset.

275
00:14:25,291 --> 00:14:26,375
So there you have it.

276
00:14:26,459 --> 00:14:27,960
I'm not guilty!

277
00:14:29,754 --> 00:14:31,047
He's dead.

278
00:14:33,215 --> 00:14:36,135
Looks like you did some serious shopping.

279
00:14:37,053 --> 00:14:38,596
But where did you get the money?

280
00:14:38,721 --> 00:14:40,639
Do you like your new teapot?

281
00:14:40,973 --> 00:14:44,310
To be honest with you,
the best tea tastes delicious

282
00:14:44,435 --> 00:14:46,729
whether it comes in a porcelain pot,

283
00:14:46,854 --> 00:14:48,481
or a tin cup.

284
00:14:49,023 --> 00:14:52,276
I know we've had
some difficult times lately.

285
00:14:52,401 --> 00:14:56,030
We've had to struggle just to get by.

286
00:14:56,489 --> 00:14:58,491
But it's nothing to be ashamed of.

287
00:14:58,616 --> 00:15:01,952
There is a simple honor in poverty.

288
00:15:02,078 --> 00:15:04,747
There's no honor for me
without the Avatar.

289
00:15:04,872 --> 00:15:05,915
Zuko...

290
00:15:07,583 --> 00:15:10,544
Even if you did capture the Avatar,

291
00:15:10,628 --> 00:15:13,881
I'm not so sure
it would solve our problems.

292
00:15:14,006 --> 00:15:15,341
Not now.

293
00:15:15,466 --> 00:15:17,051
Then there is no hope at all.

294
00:15:17,176 --> 00:15:18,844
No, Zuko!

295
00:15:18,969 --> 00:15:21,180
You must never give in to despair.

296
00:15:21,305 --> 00:15:23,891
Allow yourself to slip down that road

297
00:15:23,974 --> 00:15:26,727
and you surrender
to your lowest instincts.

298
00:15:28,145 --> 00:15:30,022
In the darkest times,

299
00:15:30,147 --> 00:15:33,400
hope is something you give yourself.

300
00:15:33,526 --> 00:15:36,987
That is the meaning of inner strength.

301
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:48,040
KATARA: Mayor Tong.

302
00:15:48,499 --> 00:15:51,001
I'd like for the court
to hear one last testimony.

303
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:55,005
I've already told you!
It's just me and the accused.

304
00:15:55,131 --> 00:15:57,508
You can't call any witnesses.

305
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:59,718
This isn't just any witness.

306
00:15:59,844 --> 00:16:01,554
I'm going to call...

307
00:16:01,679 --> 00:16:04,014
Avatar Kyoshi herself!

308
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:05,850
CROWD: ( MURMURING )

309
00:16:05,975 --> 00:16:07,351
Are they serious?

310
00:16:07,434 --> 00:16:08,561
MAN: That's impossible.

311
00:16:13,566 --> 00:16:14,733
What are you doing?

312
00:16:14,859 --> 00:16:17,069
Well, she is Aang's past life.

313
00:16:17,194 --> 00:16:19,947
Maybe wearing her stuff
will trigger something.

314
00:16:20,072 --> 00:16:23,242
I do believe in the power of stuff...

315
00:16:24,034 --> 00:16:25,536
This is a mockery of Chin law!

316
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,372
Please, if you could
just wait one more second!

317
00:16:28,497 --> 00:16:30,708
I'm sure Kyoshi will be here.

318
00:16:33,419 --> 00:16:36,630
( SPEAKING IN HIGH VOICE )
Hey, everybody. Avatar Kyoshi here.

319
00:16:36,881 --> 00:16:39,341
This is ridiculous.

320
00:16:39,550 --> 00:16:42,052
For the murder of Chin the Great,

321
00:16:42,261 --> 00:16:44,638
this court finds the Avatar...

322
00:16:55,316 --> 00:16:57,443
I killed Chin the Conqueror...

323
00:16:59,570 --> 00:17:01,280
A horrible tyrant.

324
00:17:01,405 --> 00:17:02,948
Chin was expanding his army

325
00:17:03,073 --> 00:17:05,242
to all corners of the continent.

326
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:08,954
When they came to the neck
of the peninsula where we lived,

327
00:17:09,038 --> 00:17:11,081
he demanded our immediate surrender.

328
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:15,794
I warned him that I would not
sit passively while he took our home.

329
00:17:16,378 --> 00:17:18,255
But he did not back down.

330
00:17:25,971 --> 00:17:29,516
On that day, we split from the mainland.

331
00:17:31,894 --> 00:17:36,565
( RUMBLING )

332
00:18:03,842 --> 00:18:05,719
Ahh!

333
00:18:07,221 --> 00:18:08,264
Aah!

334
00:18:08,389 --> 00:18:09,890
( SPLASHING )

335
00:18:12,142 --> 00:18:13,852
KYOSHI: I created Kyoshi island

336
00:18:13,978 --> 00:18:16,605
so my people could be safe from invaders.

337
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:25,864
Oh...

338
00:18:27,032 --> 00:18:29,952
So... What just happened?

339
00:18:30,077 --> 00:18:33,163
Uh... You kind of confessed.

340
00:18:33,289 --> 00:18:34,707
Sorry.

341
00:18:34,832 --> 00:18:37,626
And I find you guilty!

342
00:18:38,419 --> 00:18:40,963
Bring out the Wheel of Punishment!

343
00:18:41,046 --> 00:18:42,715
CROWD: ( CHEERING )

344
00:18:42,965 --> 00:18:44,300
( CHATTERS )

345
00:18:48,304 --> 00:18:49,513
Uncle...

346
00:18:49,596 --> 00:18:51,348
I thought a lot about what you said.

347
00:18:51,682 --> 00:18:53,809
You did? Good, good.

348
00:18:53,892 --> 00:18:55,477
It's helped me realize something.

349
00:18:55,602 --> 00:18:58,647
We no longer have anything to gain
by traveling together.

350
00:19:00,107 --> 00:19:01,692
I need to find my own way.

351
00:19:09,158 --> 00:19:10,743
IROH: Wait!

352
00:19:10,868 --> 00:19:11,994
( GRUNTS )

353
00:19:25,090 --> 00:19:29,011
MAN: The accused will now
Spin the Wheel of Punishment

354
00:19:29,094 --> 00:19:31,305
to determine his sentence.

355
00:19:33,724 --> 00:19:35,559
I said I would face justice,

356
00:19:35,684 --> 00:19:36,685
so I will.

357
00:19:42,441 --> 00:19:44,276
Come on torture machine!

358
00:19:44,401 --> 00:19:46,070
Eaten by bears!

359
00:19:46,195 --> 00:19:47,488
Razor pit!

360
00:19:47,613 --> 00:19:48,655
Community service!

361
00:19:48,781 --> 00:19:50,616
Please stop on community service!

362
00:19:56,163 --> 00:19:59,375
Looks like it's boiled in oil.

363
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,959
( CHEERING )

364
00:20:10,719 --> 00:20:14,431
We've come to claim
this village for the Fire Lord!

365
00:20:14,765 --> 00:20:16,892
Now show me your leader, so I may...

366
00:20:21,063 --> 00:20:22,481
Dethrone him.

367
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:25,109
- That's him over there!
-( YELPS )

368
00:20:25,234 --> 00:20:27,277
You, Avatar. Do something!

369
00:20:27,778 --> 00:20:29,655
Gee, I'd love to help,

370
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:32,074
but I'm supposed to be boiled in oil.

371
00:20:33,242 --> 00:20:34,701
There, community service.

372
00:20:34,827 --> 00:20:36,286
Now serve our community,

373
00:20:36,412 --> 00:20:38,414
and get rid of those rhinos!

374
00:20:42,501 --> 00:20:43,585
( GROWLS )

375
00:20:48,507 --> 00:20:49,591
Uh!

376
00:20:51,135 --> 00:20:52,177
( SPLASHING )

377
00:20:52,511 --> 00:20:53,887
( GROWLS )

378
00:20:54,012 --> 00:20:55,097
Ahh!

379
00:20:59,810 --> 00:21:02,187
Rough Rhinos, to the town!

380
00:21:02,312 --> 00:21:03,439
( SCREAMING )

381
00:21:11,697 --> 00:21:12,948
Ahh!

382
00:21:25,252 --> 00:21:26,336
( GASPS )

383
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:35,846
Boomerang!

384
00:21:35,971 --> 00:21:38,348
You do always come back.

385
00:21:45,063 --> 00:21:46,106
Ah!

386
00:22:10,339 --> 00:22:11,423
Uh!

387
00:22:20,933 --> 00:22:21,975
Uh!

388
00:22:25,854 --> 00:22:27,481
MAYOR: From now on,

389
00:22:27,606 --> 00:22:30,150
we'll celebrate a new Avatar Day,

390
00:22:30,275 --> 00:22:32,361
in honor of the day Avatar Aang

391
00:22:32,486 --> 00:22:35,572
saved us from the Rough Rhino invasion.

392
00:22:35,697 --> 00:22:36,990
What is this?

393
00:22:37,449 --> 00:22:39,910
MAYOR: That's our new festival food.

394
00:22:40,035 --> 00:22:42,037
Unfried dough.

395
00:22:42,162 --> 00:22:44,331
May we eat it and be reminded

396
00:22:44,456 --> 00:22:49,878
of how on this day
the Avatar was not boiled in oil.

397
00:22:50,003 --> 00:22:51,463
( CHEERING )

398
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:59,471
Happy Avatar Day, everyone.

399
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:07,020
This is by far the worst town
we've ever been to.

400
00:23:16,446 --> 00:23:18,448
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
